[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/5338840111","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3987#issuecomment-5338840111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3987","id":5338840111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABPjg8Lw","user":{"login":"jthrilly","id":1387940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODc5NDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1387940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly","html_url":"https://github.com/jthrilly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthrilly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T07:21:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:24:36Z","body":"Just to add that I came across this when working with buttons in the Toolbar component. It was very counter-intuitive to me to find that `focusableWhenDisabled` defaults to _true_ in this case, meaning that my disabled buttons still displayed hover and selected states. In my opinion, button behaviour should be consistent throughout all UI - if a native HTML button is taken out of the tab order when disabled, a button in a toolbar should not be part of roving focus.\n\nThe valid use-cases for making `focusableWhenDisabled` true is discoverability of options/commands that are currently disabled, as as well as managing focus when a currently selected button becomes disabled (for example an \"undo\" button that is clicked and there are subsequently no further undo items). In both cases the use-case is less common than the alternative IMO, and in the latter case, I think the toolbar itself could handle changing focus to the next available button in the toolbar, else falling back up a level.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/5338840111/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/5828077039","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3987#issuecomment-5828077039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3987","id":5828077039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABW2Fl7w","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-25T06: